<title>USA: TABLE - Colgate-Palmolive Q2 share rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Colgate-Palmolive Q2 share rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colgate-Palmolive Company Summary of Consolidated Results</p>
<p>Three Months and Six Months Ended June 30, 1997 and 1996</p>
<p>	     (In Millions Except Per Share Amounts) (Unaudited)</p>
<p>				     Second Quarter     First Half</p>
<p>				     1997	1996     1997     1996</p>
<p> Net Sales		    $2,300.9 $2,167.3 $4,448.0 $4,221.0</p>
<p> Cost of Sales		 1,132.8  1,106.3  2,199.3  2,156.7</p>
<p> Gross Profit		  1,168.1  1,061.0  2,248.7  2,064.3</p>
<p>Selling, General and</p>
<p> Administrative Expenses     854.6    780.5  1,628.7  1,514.3</p>
<p>Earnings Before Interest</p>
<p> and Taxes			 313.5    280.5    620.0    550.0</p>
<p> Net Interest Expense	   47.0     53.1     92.7    100.2</p>
<p>Income Before Income</p>
<p> Taxes			     266.5    227.4    527.3    449.8</p>
<p>Provision for</p>
<p> Income Taxes		     90.7     78.5    181.9    157.4</p>
<p> Net Income			175.8    148.9    345.4    292.4</p>
<p>Preferred Dividends,</p>
<p> Net of Tax			  5.2	5.3     10.6     10.7</p>
<p> Earnings Per Common Share     .58	.49     1.14	.96</p>
<p>Average Common Shares</p>
<p> Outstanding		     295.3    293.1    294.9    292.6</p>
<p>NOTE: Assuming full dilution, earnings per common share were $.54 vs. $.46 for the second quarter and $1.06 vs. $.90 for the first six months ended June 30, 1997 and 1996.</p>
<p>Average common shares outstanding assuming full dilution were 325.9 million vs 322.3 million in the second quarters and 325.8 million vs 321.9 million in the first six months. All share and per share amounts reflect the 1997 two-for-one common stock split.</p>
<p>Analysts' consensus earnings estimate for Q2 1997 was $0.56 per share, according to First Call.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
